---
// Terms for the website purchase model (22 Oct 2026): websites from £200,
// each individually quoted, optionally on a payment plan. Hosting and
// maintenance is a separate £25/month from when hosting starts (including
// during a payment plan) and never counts towards the website's price;
// customers can use their own hosting instead. Weekly backups (repository
// only, no recovery promise) are included since 23 Oct 2026 (Backblaze B2,
// EU); keep encryption details, paths and credentials off this page. Only
// settled terms
// appear here. Clauses awaiting decisions or legal review live in
// the private draft clauses (kept outside this repository), and each gap is marked with a
// <ToConfirm> (visible in development, hidden in production, and caught by
// `npm run check:publish`). Keep this page, Pricing.astro and FAQ.astro
// saying the same thing.
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import ToConfirm from "../components/ToConfirm.astro";
import { contact, business, addressNote } from "../data/config";

const lastUpdated = "22 October 2026";

const sections = [
  { id: "about", label: "About these terms" },
  { id: "who-for", label: "Business and personal buyers" },
  { id: "preview", label: "Free homepage preview" },
  { id: "quotes", label: "Quotes and accepting them" },
  { id: "payment", label: "Paying for your website" },
  { id: "ownership", label: "When the website becomes yours" },
  { id: "early", label: "Ending before it's paid for" },
  { id: "maintenance", label: "Hosting and maintenance" },
  { id: "backups", label: "Backups" },
  { id: "own-hosting", label: "Using your own hosting" },
  { id: "handover", label: "Handover" },
  { id: "after-hosting", label: "After hosting ends" },
  { id: "domain", label: "Your domain and content" },
  { id: "late", label: "If a payment is late" },
  { id: "refunds", label: "Refunds and your rights" },
  { id: "cancel-14", label: "14-day cancellation (personal buyers)" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Questions and complaints" },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms | Stapled."
  description="How buying a website from Stapled. works: quotes, payment plans, when the website becomes yours, optional £25 a month hosting and maintenance, cancelling and handover."
  path="/terms/"
  heading="Terms"
  intro="How buying a website from me works, in plain English: what you pay, when it's yours, and how to leave."
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="about">
    <h2>About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are between you and {business.proprietor}, a sole trader
      trading as {business.tradingAs} ("I" or "me"), based in Southampton,
      UK. You can reach me at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
    </p>
    {business.address ? (
      <p>
        My {business.addressLabel.toLowerCase()} is {business.address}. It's
        for post and formal documents only, not an office open to visitors.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <ToConfirm note={addressNote} />
    )}
    <p>
      They apply alongside the written quote I send you. When you accept a
      quote by email, the quote and these terms (in the version dated on
      this page) make up our agreement. If you agreed a different
      arrangement with me before {lastUpdated}, that arrangement still
      applies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="who-for">
    <h2>Business and personal buyers</h2>
    <p>
      I work with businesses and with individuals. Some parts of these
      terms depend on which you are, because the law gives extra protection
      to people buying for personal use.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Buying for a business:</strong> you're buying mainly for your
        trade, business or profession. That includes sole traders and
        partnerships buying for their business.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Buying for personal use:</strong> you're buying mainly for
        purposes outside any trade or business. The law calls you a
        "consumer", and the parts marked "personal buyers" apply to you.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="preview">
    <h2>Free homepage preview</h2>
    <p>
      If you ask for one, I'll put together a first look at how your
      homepage could feel and read, based on what you've told me. It's
      free, and you're under no obligation to go ahead afterwards.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="quotes">
    <h2>Quotes and accepting them</h2>
    <p>Before any work starts, I'll email you a quote that sets out:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>what the website will include</li>
      <li>its total purchase price</li>
      <li>if you'd like to spread the cost, the payment schedule we've agreed</li>
      <li>whether I'll host it (and the £25 a month that costs) or you'll use your own hosting</li>
      <li>whether you're buying for a business or for personal use</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You accept a quote by replying to say so. Nothing is payable until you
      do. Any extra work you ask for later is quoted separately and only
      goes ahead if you agree.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="payment">
    <h2>Paying for your website</h2>
    <p>
      Websites start from £200. Your quote sets your website's total price.
      You can pay it in one go, or spread it with a payment plan: the
      payment schedule we agree is set out in your quote.
    </p>
    <p>
      Payments are made by bank transfer. I'll send you the details with
      your quote. I'm not registered for VAT, so no VAT is added to any
      price.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you're on a payment plan, you can pay the remaining balance at any
      time to finish paying early.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ownership">
    <h2>When the website becomes yours</h2>
    <p>
      Once you've paid the full price, the website is yours. I transfer the
      website's files to you, along with the rights I own in its design and
      code.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some parts of a website may be licensed from someone else, such as a
      stock photo, a font or a third-party service, rather than owned by me.
      If anything in your website comes with licence restrictions, I'll tell
      you what they are before you accept your quote.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="early">
    <h2>Ending before your website is paid for</h2>
    <p>You have two options if you want to stop before the price is paid:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Finish paying:</strong> pay the remaining balance, and the
        website and its transferable files are yours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>End the agreement early:</strong> give me one calendar
        month's notice by email. Payment-plan instalments that fall due
        during the notice period are still payable, and they count towards
        the website's price. If I'm hosting the website, hosting ends when
        the notice period ends, and the £25 monthly fee is payable until
        then. If you end early,
        the website and its files aren't transferred to you, but your domain
        and the content you gave me are still yours.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Personal buyers also have the 14-day cancellation right described{" "}
      <a href="#cancel-14">below</a>.
    </p>
  </section>


  <section id="maintenance">
    <h2>Hosting and maintenance</h2>
    <p>
      If you'd like me to host your website, hosting and maintenance costs
      £25 a month. It's a separate, rolling monthly arrangement:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        It starts when I start hosting your website, including while you're
        still paying for the website on a payment plan.
      </li>
      <li>
        It's separate from the website's price and doesn't count towards
        paying it off.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>It includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>hosting, with HTTPS</li>
      <li>
        technical maintenance, such as keeping the site's software up to date
        and fixing faults in code I've written
      </li>
      <li>
        weekly backups of your website's code and files stored in its
        repository (see <a href="#backups">backups</a>)
      </li>
      <li>
        up to 30 minutes of minor content edits a month, such as changing
        text, prices, opening hours or photos on existing pages. Unused time
        doesn't carry over to the next month.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      New pages, redesigns and new features aren't included. I'll quote for
      them separately, and they only go ahead if you agree.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can cancel hosting and maintenance at any time by giving one
      calendar month's notice by email. Hosting continues until the end of
      that notice period, which you pay for as normal, and then ends.
      Cancelling hosting never means losing a website you've already paid
      for, and it doesn't cancel any payment-plan instalments still due for
      the website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="backups">
    <h2>Backups</h2>
    <p>
      While I host your website, I back up its code and the files stored in
      its repository once a week, and keep the copies with a cloud storage
      service.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Timing:</strong> backups are scheduled weekly. If the
        computer that runs them is switched off, asleep or offline, a backup
        may run late, and is taken as soon as it's next available. A missed
        week isn't recreated afterwards.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Upload:</strong> a backup needs that computer to be connected
        to the internet and the storage service to be available. If an upload
        fails, it's retried, and otherwise tried again at the next daily
        check.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What's covered:</strong> the website's code and the files
        saved in its repository.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What isn't covered:</strong> databases, emails, third-party
        services (such as booking or form tools), account settings (such as
        your domain registrar account), passwords and other secrets, and any
        changes that haven't been saved to the repository.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>How long copies are kept:</strong> weekly copies for about 8
        weeks and one copy a month for about 6 months. After that they're
        removed automatically and permanently deleted within a further 30
        days.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Backups make it possible for me to try to restore your website if
      something goes wrong. I can't guarantee that a restore will succeed,
      or how long it will take. That doesn't change my duty to provide
      hosting, maintenance and backups with reasonable care and skill, or
      any of your rights under the law (see{" "}
      <a href="#refunds">refunds and your rights</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="own-hosting">
    <h2>Using your own hosting</h2>
    <p>
      You don't have to host with me. If you use your own hosting, you pay
      me no monthly hosting fee, and I'll provide the transferable website
      files and basic setup instructions as set out in your quote.
    </p>
    <p>
      Choosing your own hosting doesn't cancel any payments still due for
      your website, and ownership only passes to you once the website is
      fully paid for, as described in{" "}
      <a href="#ownership">when the website becomes yours</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="handover">
    <h2>Handover</h2>
    <p>
      When I'm hosting a website you've paid for and that hosting is ending,
      I'll send you, before hosting ends:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>a ZIP file of the website's transferable files</li>
      <li>basic instructions for putting it online with another host</li>
      <li>
        a note of anything that needs moving separately or can't be
        transferred, such as a database, a third-party service, a licence
        or an account in my name
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="after-hosting">
    <h2>After hosting ends</h2>
    <p>
      Once hosting has ended and the handover is complete, I keep a recovery
      copy of your website for 30 days, in case anything goes wrong with the
      move. After that I delete it from my active storage. Backup copies
      made while I was hosting your website are deleted automatically when
      they reach the end of the retention periods in{" "}
      <a href="#backups">backups</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      This doesn't cover business records I have to keep, such as quotes,
      agreements and invoices. Those are kept for the periods set out in the
      <a href="/privacy/#retention">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="domain">
    <h2>Your domain and content</h2>
    <p>
      Your domain, photos, text and logo are always yours, whatever happens.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>If you already have a domain,</strong> you keep it and stay
        in control of it. I only need enough access to point it at your
        website.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>If you need a new one,</strong> I'll register it with you as
        the named owner (the registrant).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cost:</strong> while I host your website, including while
        you're paying for it, I include up to £20 a year towards the domain.
        If it costs more than that, I'll agree the extra with you before
        buying or renewing it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>When hosting with me ends,</strong> I'll help you take over
        the domain: either by moving it into a registrar account of your
        own, or by giving you its transfer code so you can move it to
        another provider. From then on, renewing it is up to you.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="late">
    <h2>If a payment is late</h2>
    <ol class="pp-steps">
      <li>
        I'll email you a reminder saying what's overdue and the date hosting
        will be suspended if it's still unpaid. That date will be at least
        14 days after the reminder.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you pay before then, nothing else happens. If something's wrong,
        reply to the reminder and we'll sort it out.
      </li>
      <li>
        If it's still unpaid on that date and I'm hosting your website, I'll
        suspend hosting, which takes the website offline.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Suspension is temporary. It doesn't delete your website, it doesn't
      end our agreement, and it doesn't add any charges. Once the overdue
      amount is paid, I'll put the website back online.
    </p>
    <p>
      Suspending hosting, ending the agreement and deleting data are three
      separate things. The agreement only ends as described in these terms,
      and website data is only deleted as described in{" "}
      <a href="#after-hosting">after hosting ends</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="refunds">
    <h2>Refunds and your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Whether you buy for a business or for personal use, the law requires
      my work to be carried out with reasonable care and skill. If something
      isn't, tell me and I'll put it right. If that isn't possible, you may
      be entitled to a price reduction or a refund.
    </p>
    <p>
      Beyond those rights, I don't offer an extra refund if you simply change
      your mind about work that's been completed and supplied properly.
      Nothing in these terms takes away or limits any rights you have by
      law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cancel-14">
    <h2>14-day cancellation (personal buyers)</h2>
    <p>
      If you're buying for personal use and you accept a quote by email,
      phone or anywhere other than my business premises, you can cancel
      within 14 days of accepting it. You don't need to give a reason. To
      cancel, email me at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> with a clear
      statement that you're cancelling.
    </p>
    <p>
      I won't start work during those 14 days unless you ask me to in
      writing. If you ask me to start and then cancel within the 14 days,
      you pay a proportionate amount for the work done up to when you tell
      me you're cancelling, and I'll refund anything you've paid beyond that
      within 14 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you ask me to start early and the work is completely finished
      within the 14 days, you lose the right to cancel once it's finished,
      but only if you confirmed in writing, when asking me to start, that
      you understood this.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If something isn't right, email me at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> and I'll do my
      best to sort it out. For how I handle your personal information, see
      the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    {business.address ? (
      <p>
        You can also write to me at my{" "}
        {business.addressLabel.toLowerCase()}: {business.address}.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <ToConfirm note={addressNote} />
    )}
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
